    <comment>Number box label: the GPU core clock offset, in MHz.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="GpuClocks_Memory.Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Memoria (MHz)</value>
    <comment>Number box label: the GPU memory clock offset, in MHz.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="GpuClocks_Footer.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Gli offset della memoria contano doppio, come in MSI Afterburner: +100 alza la frequenza della memoria di 50 MHz.</value>
    <comment>Note under the GPU overclock rows. MSI Afterburner is a product name.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="GpuClocks_Always" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Sempre</value>
    <comment>The only row of GPU offsets on laptops without operating modes: they apply all the time.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="GpuClocks_InUse" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>In uso ora</value>
    <comment>Under the operating mode whose GPU offsets apply right now.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="GpuClocks_Firmware" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Di Acer: core {0} MHz, memoria {1} MHz</value>
    <comment>Under an operating mode in the GPU overclock section: the firmware's own offsets for that mode. {0} = core offset, {1} = memory offset (signed numbers, e.g. +150).</comment>
  </data>
